[13:07:58][handy_keys] hotkey=alt_right, state=Released
[13:07:58][transcription_coordinator][WARN] Transcription coordinator channel closed
[13:08:15][utils][INFO] Initiating operation cancellation...
```

Observations:

1. `tray icon error: 未指定的错误 (os error -2147467259)` is `0x80004005` / `E_FAIL` from the tray/icon path, and it repeats on every recording-state update.
2. The coordinator panic happens in the same second as the tray failures.
3. The panic payload is logged as `Any { .. }`, so the actual panic message is lost — `Box<dyn Any>`'s `Debug` never prints the inner `&str`/`String`. This is why this report cannot point at the root cause.
4. Afterwards the process is no longer present: `Get-Process handy` returns nothing, so this is not just a wedged channel — the app exits.
5. Note that the ASR model load finishes on its own (`Successfully loaded transcription model ... took 5817ms`) a few seconds after the panic, so model load is not what fails; it is a bystander in this sequence.

The user-visible symptom is "pressing the hotkey did nothing for a long time and then Handy was gone", and while it was still alive the UI felt sluggish (the machine also had very little free RAM at that moment: ~5.5 GB free of 31.5 GB with the ASR model resident).

## Steps to Reproduce

Not deterministic in my testing — it happened on the first dictation after the machine had been idle for hours (possibly after sleep/resume), with the app running since a previous session.

Rough sequence:

1. Windows 11 machine, Handy running in the background (tray icon disabled in settings, `model_unload_timeout = never`).
2. Leave the machine idle for hours, or resume from sleep.
3. Press the dictation hotkey once (right Alt, toggle mode).
4. Tray icon updates fail with `E_FAIL`, the transformer coordinator panics, and no text is produced.

## Expected Behavior

- The coordinator should not be able to die from a failed tray update. If tray/UI work fails, it should be reported and skipped, not propagated into the transcription path.
- Even if the coordinator does panic, the app should survive (the panic happens inside a spawned task; the current behaviour leaves a closed channel and, in this case, the process exited).

