## Evidence that it was really running on the iGPU

- **Windows per-process GPU memory counters** (`\GPU Process Memory(pid_<handy>_*)`), taken after the idle unload (the ggml device stays alive): handy.exe held **0 MB on the NVIDIA adapter and 15.7 MB on the Intel adapter**. After the workaround below, handy.exe shows 1.6 GB on the NVIDIA adapter while the model is loaded, and nothing on the Intel adapter.
