## A follow-up experiment: the empty block is the actual cause

I then isolated the variable. 10 phrases × 2 runs each, same request shape, `gemma-4-31b-it` / `gemma-4-26b-a4b-it`:

| Variant | System message | User message | Empty results (31B) | Empty results (26B) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| A (as sent today) | has the empty `<transcript></transcript>` block + "The above is a transcript…" | bare text | **8 / 20** | **2 / 20** |
| B | same as A | text wrapped in `<transcript>` tags | 0 / 20 | 0 / 20 |
| F | no empty block; "The above is a transcript" → "The user message is a transcript" | text wrapped in tags | 0 / 20 | 0 / 20 |
| G | same as F | bare text | 0 / 20 | 0 / 20 |

So the delimiting tags are not required; what breaks things is the dangling, empty `<transcript></transcript>` block together with "The above is a transcript…" pointing at nothing. Removing it fixes the problem with no other change.

## Proposed fix

